# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Your machine's settings, which `.cargo/config.toml` includes and this repository therefore never
# holds. It is where the Wi-Fi credentials for the proof of concept live: the firmware has no
# filesystem to read them from, so they are compiled into it, and a tracked file would make the
# password a matter of record — in the repository as well as in the flash image.
.cargo/local.toml

# Node tooling for the quality gate: installed by `npm run setup`, pinned by package-lock.json.
# Everything else in this file's absence would be a gate failure rather than an inconvenience, because
# markdownlint, cspell and editorconfig-checker all read tracked files, so this line is load-bearing
# rather than cosmetic.
node_modules/
.cspellcache

# Editor configuration
# .vscode/ is NOT ignored, and deliberately so: the formatter and linter settings in it are how the
# editor and `npm run check` end up reading the same configuration. .zed/, .helix/ and .nvim.lua are
# still ignored because there is no equivalent to check in.
.zed/
.helix/
.nvim.lua

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Ignore .DS_Store file in mac
**/.DS_Store
